# Bench corpus — seeded defects in this repo, scored by this repo's own checks.
#
# One JSON object per line (blank lines and '#' comments skipped), matching the
# eval corpus convention in tests/eval/corpus/seed.jsonl. Each task's defect is
# tests/bench/patches/<id>.patch, applied to a pristine sandbox copy.
#
# Every task here was validated empirically: the defect makes `suite` fail, and
# reversing it makes `suite` pass. `bun scripts/bench.ts validate` re-proves it.
# Candidates that broke nothing were dropped rather than shipped as tasks.
#
# The split into dev/sealed is NOT chosen here — it is derived from each id and
# the committed SEAL_SALT. Do not rename an id to move it.
{"id":"ema-alpha-weights","title":"EMA update weights the wrong term","prompt":"The core test suite fails: `EMA scoring > emaUpdate with alpha=0.3` expects an update that leans on the existing score, but gets a value that leans on the new observation instead. Something in the crafted-tool scoring path is wrong. Find it and fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/craft/ema.ts"],"tags":["arithmetic","craft"]}
{"id":"ema-decay-inverted","title":"Time decay grows instead of decaying","prompt":"Five tests in the core suite fail, including `Time decay > 60 days → quarter score` and `filterByEffectiveScore — the one injection policy > time decay retires a once-good tool`. Crafted tools that have not been used in a long time are not losing score the way the suite expects. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/craft/ema.ts"],"tags":["arithmetic","craft","decay"]}
{"id":"mcts-reward-clamp","title":"MCTS reward clamp collapses every reward","prompt":"Eight tests fail across `Backpropagation` and `MCTS integration`, e.g. `Backpropagation > running mean after two updates` and `a branch whose code FAILS execution scores below a branch whose code PASSES`. Node values are not tracking the rewards being backpropagated. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/backpropagation.ts"],"tags":["mcts","bounds"]}
{"id":"outcome-quality-swap","title":"Feedback maps to inverted quality","prompt":"The core suite fails: `EvolutionEngine.reviewTurn — the outcome signal > craft EMA moves on outcomes: corrected pushes a tool score down, accepted up`. Tool scores are moving in the opposite direction from the user feedback that caused them. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","outcomes"]}
{"id":"outcome-abandoned-feedback","title":"Abandoned turns are treated as negative signal","prompt":"Two core tests fail, including `outcome mappings > outcomeToFeedback` and `no follow-up (session end): abandoned, neutral, no reflection unless errored`. A turn the user simply walked away from is being scored as though they disliked it. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","outcomes"]}
{"id":"trivial-turn-toolcalls","title":"Turns that ran tools are classified as trivial","prompt":"Three core tests fail, including `isTrivialTurn — the LLM-call pre-filter > a turn that ran tools is never trivial`. The pre-filter that decides whether a turn is worth classifying is reaching the wrong conclusion about turns with tool calls. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","filter"]}
{"id":"shadow-regression-veto","title":"Regression veto fires one loss too early","prompt":"Two core tests fail: `decidePromotion > tolerates one loss (maxRegressions=1, Monte-Carlo settled) but vetoes the second` and `a tolerant config (maxRegressions>0) permits promotion despite some losses`. The shadow-rollout veto is rejecting scaffold variants that the configured tolerance should have allowed through. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/scaffold/shadow.ts"],"tags":["scaffold","shadow","boundary"]}
{"id":"archive-novelty-bonus","title":"Archive exploration weight rewards trials instead of novelty","prompt":"The core suite fails: `selectEvolutionBase — the exploration-share policy > explore weighting favors high win-rate and novel (untried) variants`. The DGM-style archive sampler is preferring heavily-tried variants when it should be preferring ones we know least about. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/scaffold/archive.ts"],"tags":["scaffold","archive","exploration"]}
{"id":"eval-gate-boundary","title":"Quality gate rejects a score exactly at the threshold","prompt":"The core suite fails: `evaluateGate > boundary: aggregate exactly at threshold passes`. A run that lands exactly on the committed quality floor is being failed. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/eval/report.ts"],"tags":["eval","boundary"]}
{"id":"eval-gate-empty-corpus","title":"Empty corpus silently passes the quality gate","prompt":"The core suite fails: `evaluateGate > empty corpus fails the gate (proves nothing)`. A benchmark run with zero cases is being allowed through the gate instead of being rejected. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/eval/report.ts"],"tags":["eval","degenerate"]}
{"id":"misevolution-egress","title":"Misevolution gate no longer catches one egress channel","prompt":"Five core tests fail, including `checkMisevolution — the fixed criteria > vetoes network-egress` and `a proposal that opens raw egress is refused at gate 1 with a recorded reason`. The safety gate over evolved artifacts has a hole: one way of reaching the network is no longer detected. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/scaffold/misevolution.ts"],"tags":["safety","misevolution"]}
{"id":"turnfail-oversize-ratio","title":"Oversized-prompt heuristic never triggers","prompt":"The core suite fails: `classifyTurnFailure > size heuristic: a rate limit at >50% window on the PER-REQUEST prompt is context-class`. A provider rate-limit that arrives on a very large prompt should be recognised as a context-size problem, and it no longer is. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/turn-failure.ts"],"tags":["failure-classification","heuristic"]}
{"id":"turnfail-default-class","title":"Unrecognised failures default to the wrong class","prompt":"Two core tests fail: `classifyTurnFailure > transient: anything else stays unclassified noise` and `planOverflowRecovery > rate limits and transient failures never force-compact`. Errors that match none of the known patterns are being given a specific classification instead of the catch-all, which then drives the wrong recovery. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/turn-failure.ts"],"tags":["failure-classification","default"]}
{"id":"pareto-strict-max","title":"Pareto front drops tied candidates","prompt":"Two core tests fail: `computeParetoFront > ties on an instance both appear in perInstanceBest` and `parentSelectionWeights + sampleParentByWeight > falls back to bestAggregate when no Pareto signal yet`. When two GEPA candidates score identically on an instance, only one of them is being kept as a best. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/gepa/pareto.ts"],"tags":["gepa","pareto","ties"]}
{"id":"outcome-frustrated-quality","title":"Frustrated turns score as high quality","prompt":"The core suite fails: `outcome mappings > outcomeQuality ties to the explicit-feedback constants`. A turn the user was visibly frustrated by is being scored as though it went well. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","outcomes"]}
{"id":"trivial-msg-length","title":"Trivial-turn filter swallows real requests","prompt":"The core suite fails: `isTrivialTurn — the LLM-call pre-filter > real requests are not trivial, even short ones with a question`. The pre-filter is classifying genuine user requests as small talk, so they never get classified. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","filter","threshold"]}
{"id":"eval-summary-average","title":"Eval averages are computed over the wrong denominator","prompt":"Two core tests fail: `eval runner > summarizeEval computes wins/ties/avgs` and `buildEvalReport > flattens results + computes aggregate/regression`. The baseline strategy's mean score comes out slightly low, which drags the reported regression delta with it. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/eval/types.ts"],"tags":["eval","arithmetic"]}
{"id":"step-prune-error-kind-lost","title":"Truncated tool failures come back as successes","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `pruneStepToolOutputs > error outputs keep error semantics through truncation`. When a step's context goes over budget and an old tool result is shrunk, a failed tool call is handed back to the model looking like an ordinary successful one. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/step-prune.ts"],"tags":["step-prune","operator"]}
{"id":"step-prune-recent-budget-cost","title":"Recent-tool budget protects one result too many","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `pruneStepToolOutputs > over budget → OLD tool outputs shrink to head + marker, recent budget stays verbatim` and `pruneStepToolOutputs > byte-stable across steps: a grown array re-truncates old parts to identical bytes`. The intra-turn pruner keeps more recent tool results verbatim than its recent-output token budget allows, so an output that should have shrunk stays full size. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/step-prune.ts"],"tags":["step-prune","boundary"]}
{"id":"step-prune-marker-size","title":"Truncation marker misreports the original output size","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `pruneStepToolOutputs > over budget → OLD tool outputs shrink to head + marker, recent budget stays verbatim`. When an old tool output is shrunk mid-turn, the note left in its place tells the model the wrong size for the output that was cut. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/step-prune.ts"],"tags":["step-prune","arithmetic"]}
{"id":"cache-tail-breakpoint-count","title":"Tail cache breakpoints overrun the per-request budget","prompt":"Ten tests in the core suite fail, including `markCacheTail > marks exactly the last 2 non-system messages` and `markCacheTail > total anthropic breakpoints (tool + system + tail) stay within the API limit`. The prompt-cache layer rolls more breakpoints onto the message tail than the provider's per-request budget leaves for it once the tool surface and the system prompt have taken their share. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/cache-breakpoints.ts"],"tags":["prompt-cache","boundary"]}
{"id":"cache-stale-marker-kept","title":"Stale cache markers are never stripped when the tail rolls","prompt":"Four tests in the core suite fail, including `markCacheTail > rolls forward: stale markers deeper in the conversation are stripped` and `markCacheTail > preserves unrelated providerOptions while stripping/re-marking`. Re-rolling the cache breakpoints for a new step leaves the previous step's markers in place, so they pile up deeper and deeper in the conversation. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/cache-breakpoints.ts"],"tags":["prompt-cache","operator"]}
{"id":"cache-openrouter-model-dialect","title":"OpenRouter cache dialect is decided from the wrong identifier","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `resolvePromptCacheStrategy > openrouter gets cache_control markers only for Anthropic models` and `OpenRouter cache addressing on the wire > claude behind openrouter: prompt_cache_key + cache_control on system and tail`. Routing through an aggregator no longer notices when the model behind it speaks the Anthropic cache dialect, so those requests lose their per-message breakpoints entirely. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/cache-breakpoints.ts"],"tags":["prompt-cache","default"]}
{"id":"prepare-step-marks-unpruned","title":"Step pipeline discards its own pruning before the request goes out","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `composePrepareStep with pruning > cache markers land LAST, on the pruned array`. In the shared per-step pipeline the step-boundary tool-output pruning is computed and then thrown away whenever a prompt-cache plan is active, so an over-budget turn keeps re-sending its full tool traffic. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/prepare-step.ts"],"tags":["prepare-step","ordering"]}
{"id":"step-injection-replay-base-sign","title":"Mid-turn injections replay at the wrong durable-history offset","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail, including `StepInjections > replayInto splices the injections at the positions the model saw, in response coordinates`. Messages injected mid-turn are merged back into the turn's response at the wrong offsets, so the persisted transcript no longer matches the order the model actually saw. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/step-injections.ts"],"tags":["step-injections","arithmetic"]}
{"id":"structured-json-drops-closer","title":"JSON extracted from model prose is cut short and fails to parse","prompt":"Over thirty tests across the core suite fail, including `structured prompt helpers > extracts balanced JSON objects with nested braces and strings` and `Voyager curriculum proposer > parses LLM response + filters by learnability window`. Every consumer that pulls a structured payload out of a model's prose reply now gets a parse error instead. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompts/structured.ts"],"tags":["structured-output","boundary"]}
{"id":"surface-workspace-selectable-flip","title":"The internal workspace runtime is no longer selectable","prompt":"Four tests in the core suite fail, including `buildSystemPromptSync > renders executor section when registeredExecutors supplied` and `buildSystemPromptSync > prompt surface hides unavailable executors from selectable runtimes`. The always-present internal state runtime drops out of the prompt's selectable execution environments, so the model is told it cannot use the one runtime that is always there. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/surface.ts"],"tags":["prompt-surface","guard"]}
{"id":"profile-reasoning-heuristic-and","title":"Id-only capability fallback stops recognising reasoning-only models","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `buildSystemPromptSync > model profile blocks tool mode on known non-tool models`. When a caller passes only a model id and no catalog entry, the capability fallback no longer recognises the known reasoning-only models, so they are advertised as tool-capable and agent mode is allowed to start on them. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/model-profile.ts"],"tags":["model-profile","operator"]}
{"id":"agentsmd-budget-order-rootmost","title":"AGENTS.md size cap is spent in the wrong precedence order","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `renderAgentsMdSection > spends the cap nearest-first: the nearest file survives a giant root file` and `renderAgentsMdSection > omits a broader file outright when the leftover budget is useless`. The project-instructions block spends its character cap against the wrong end of the precedence chain, so a large repo-root file can crowd out the instructions closest to the working directory. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/agents-md.ts"],"tags":["agents-md","ordering"]}
{"id":"attach-vfs-exists-not-awaited","title":"Replaced attachments are never written to the workspace","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `sanitizeAttachmentsForModel > replaces a PDF for a text-only model with a VFS reference and writes the exact bytes once` and `sanitizeAttachmentsForModel > large text/* attachments get the VFS treatment`. An attachment the model cannot accept is swapped for a workspace path as intended, but the payload never lands there, so the path the agent is told to read points at nothing. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/attachment-sanitizer.ts"],"tags":["attachments","async"]}
{"id":"attach-ceiling-ignored","title":"Attachment policy trusts the catalog past the transport ceiling","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `acceptedMediaForModel > workers-ai (openai-compatible wire) is capped to image even if the catalog claims pdf`. The attachment policy takes the model catalog's word for what it can receive without holding it to what the provider's wire format can actually carry, which is exactly how a document part reaches an endpoint that rejects the whole request. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/attachment-sanitizer.ts"],"tags":["attachments","operator"]}
{"id":"ledger-append-gate-inverted","title":"Ephemeral state ledger appends on the wrong condition","prompt":"Ten tests in the core suite fail, including `EphemeralContextLedger (the cache-stability contract) > (a) empty ledger + first turn → exactly one block at the tail` and `(c) fingerprint change → a SECOND block appends at the new tail; the first stays put`. The ephemeral system-state ledger never conveys a genuinely changed state to the model, while turns where nothing changed keep growing the conversation. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompting/volatile-context.ts"],"tags":["ephemeral-ledger","guard"]}
{"id":"prompt-current-date-slice","title":"System prompt's current date is no longer date-only","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `buildSystemPromptSync > renders the date-only current date in runtime context`. The date handed to the model in the runtime-context block carries more than the calendar date, which also breaks the within-a-day byte stability the cached system prefix depends on. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompt.ts"],"tags":["system-prompt","boundary"]}
{"id":"prompt-offline-laptop-inverted","title":"A registered-but-offline user PC loses its reconnect note","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `buildSystemPromptSync > a registered-but-offline laptop stays visible with the reconnect instruction` and `buildSystemPromptSync > per-section char budgets stay pinned (additions must be deliberate)`. A user machine that is registered but not currently connected is no longer surfaced in the execution-environments section, so the model can neither see it nor tell the user how to bring it back. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/prompt.ts"],"tags":["system-prompt","guard"]}
{"id":"strip-preamble-scans-last-blank-line","title":"Recovering a stored compaction checkpoint returns only its tail","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `checkpoint preamble > wrap → strip round-trips the summary body`. Recovering the body of a stored compaction checkpoint no longer round-trips — most of the handoff summary is discarded along with the header, leaving only its final fragment, so an iterative compaction update rebuilds on almost nothing. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/compaction.ts"],"tags":["compaction","boundary"]}
{"id":"latest-ask-cap-off-by-one","title":"The verbatim latest-ask block overshoots its size cap","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail, including `buildCompactionSummaryPrompt > an oversize latest ask is capped, not dropped` and `layer gate — baseline > the pipeline conforms to the locked baseline`. When a very long user request is handed to the compaction summarizer for verbatim copying, the truncated copy overshoots the size cap it is supposed to respect. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/compaction.ts"],"tags":["compaction","boundary"]}
{"id":"kimi-window-generations-swapped","title":"The static window fallback sizes the Kimi generations wrongly","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail, including `model fallbacks track new releases > Kimi context windows by generation` and `layer gate — baseline > the pipeline conforms to the locked baseline`. With no live model catalog, the static context-window fallback reports the wrong window for the Kimi generations, so a session on one of them budgets its context — and triggers compaction — against a window the model does not have. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/context-window.ts"],"tags":["context-window","default"]}
{"id":"claude-long-context-generation-dropped","title":"A long-context Claude generation falls back to the ordinary window","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `layer gate — baseline > the pipeline conforms to the locked baseline`, drifting on the `context-budget/window-table` probe. The static context-window fallback stopped recognizing one of the long-context Claude generations, so it now sizes that model at the ordinary Claude window and would compact its conversations far earlier than necessary. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/context-window.ts"],"tags":["context-window","default"]}
{"id":"drain-debounce-stops-coalescing","title":"An event burst no longer coalesces into one drain","prompt":"Four tests in the core suite fail, including `DrainScheduler — fixed-window debounce > a burst of schedule() calls in one window arms ONE timer → ONE drain` and `AgentOrchestrator.scheduleDrain — debounced ingress coalescing > an event burst schedules ONE window that drains into ONE turn`. A burst of external events no longer coalesces: every arrival opens its own drain window instead of being absorbed by the one already running, fragmenting a single cause into many turns. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/drain-scheduler.ts"],"tags":["drain","guard"]}
{"id":"drain-window-disarm-ordering","title":"An event landing mid-drain is silently swallowed","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `DrainScheduler — fixed-window debounce > the window disarms before the drain runs, so a mid-drain schedule() arms a new one`. An event that arrives while a drain is already in flight is lost to the debounce: it is too late to join that drain, and it does not open a window of its own either. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/drain-scheduler.ts"],"tags":["drain","ordering"]}
{"id":"injected-step-shows-standalone-text","title":"Mid-turn injection shows the standalone-turn wording","prompt":"Five tests in the core suite fail, including `EventInjectionBuffer > a buffered batch splices at the next step tail and stays at its entry index across steps` and `EventInjectionBuffer > batches buffered together merge into ONE user message; all count as absorbed`. When a background-event batch is spliced into a live turn, the model is shown the rendering written for a standalone event turn rather than the one written for mid-turn delivery. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/event-injection.ts"],"tags":["event-injection","wrong-field"]}
{"id":"continuation-retention-defaults-off","title":"A continuation turn stops re-absorbing the settled batches","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `EventInjectionBuffer > a CONTINUATION turn re-absorbs the just-settled batches (parity with the durable drain message)`. A turn that continues after an auto-continue or a recovery no longer re-sees the background events the previous segment had absorbed, so those events drop out of the model's view mid-answer instead of riding into the continuation. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/event-injection.ts"],"tags":["event-injection","default"]}
{"id":"single-batch-never-injects","title":"A lone buffered event batch never reaches the model","prompt":"Four tests in the core suite fail, including `EventInjectionBuffer > a buffered batch splices at the next step tail and stays at its entry index across steps` and `EventInjectionBuffer > a CONTINUATION turn re-absorbs the just-settled batches (parity with the durable drain message)`. A single buffered background-event batch never reaches the model at the next step boundary, even though it is recorded as absorbed and so is never re-enqueued either. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/event-injection.ts"],"tags":["event-injection","boundary"]}
{"id":"usageless-step-erases-prompt-size","title":"A step reporting no usage wipes the measured prompt size","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `TurnAccumulator > lastPromptTokens tracks the newest reporting step and survives usage-less steps`. A trailing step whose provider reported no usage erases the turn's measured prompt size instead of leaving the last real measurement standing, so the next turn's compaction trigger reads zero. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/turn-accumulator.ts"],"tags":["turn-accounting","degenerate"]}
{"id":"cached-tokens-subtracted-from-input","title":"Cache-read tokens are missing from the turn's input total","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `TurnAccumulator > recordStep accumulates usage across steps incl. anthropic cache-read`. The turn's accumulated input-token total comes out short whenever part of the prompt was served from the provider's cache, so a well-cached turn under-reports how big its prompt actually was. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/turn-accumulator.ts"],"tags":["turn-accounting","arithmetic"]}
{"id":"session-reflection-cadence-slips","title":"Session reflection misses the configured cadence","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `AgentOrchestrator.recordTurn — session cadence > session reflection fires every N turns`. Session-level evolution no longer runs on the configured cadence: the reflection window does not close when it reaches the configured number of turns, so each reflection covers the wrong span and the window rolls over out of step. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/agent-orchestrator.ts"],"tags":["orchestrator","boundary"]}
{"id":"programmatic-turn-displaces-pending-review","title":"A programmatic turn displaces the user turn awaiting its verdict","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `AgentOrchestrator — turn-outcome review dispatch > programmatic turns review immediately with no follow-up and do not displace the pending user turn`. A programmatic turn (a reactor drain, a job wake) now takes over the review slot that a user-origin turn was holding while it waited for the user's follow-up, so the user's next message grades the wrong turn and the real one is never graded. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/agent-orchestrator.ts"],"tags":["orchestrator","guard"]}
{"id":"mid-turn-batch-rendering-swapped","title":"A live turn is told the events arrived while it was idle","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `AgentOrchestrator.drainPendingEvents — the reactor (drain-then-stop) > an ACTIVE turn absorbs the batch mid-turn — no new turn is enqueued`. When the reactor hands a drained batch to a turn that is already running, the live turn is told the events arrived while it was idle and asked to act on each and stop, while the wording meant for that live turn is what gets kept for the standalone fallback. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/orchestrator/agent-orchestrator.ts"],"tags":["orchestrator","swapped-args"]}
{"id":"mcts-uct-depth-cap-off-by-one","title":"Tree selection still returns nodes that already sit at the depth cap","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail: `UCT selection > WP-A4: depth-capped nodes are skipped, not fatal — a shallower node is still selected` and `UCT selection > WP-A4: returns null only when every open node is at/beyond the cap`. Tree selection is handing back nodes that have already reached the configured depth limit, so the search keeps spending budget on a frontier that can no longer produce in-bounds children. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/uct.ts"],"tags":["mcts","uct","boundary"]}
{"id":"mcts-cost-undercounts-evaluation","title":"Pre-flight cost estimate ignores how many branches each iteration evaluates","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail: `Cost estimation > calculates correct total calls` and `Cost estimation > evaluation spend scales with the per-evaluation budget knob`. The pre-flight estimate no longer accounts for every branch an iteration scores, so the spend gate is told a search is much cheaper than it really is. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/cost.ts"],"tags":["mcts","cost","arithmetic"]}
{"id":"mcts-branch-listed-as-its-own-sibling","title":"A branch is told to differ from an angle list that contains its own angle","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail: `diversity angles > each branch in an N-way expansion is handed every OTHER branch angle` and `MCTS integration > DO-NOW #1: sibling diversity — each branch in an expansion gets a DISTINCT prompt naming the other branch angles`. Each branch of a parallel expansion is now handed a sibling list that includes the very approach it was itself assigned, so the branches stop being pushed apart and the parallel proposals collapse toward duplicates. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/diversity.ts"],"tags":["mcts","diversity","guard"]}
{"id":"mcts-inherited-context-drops-a-message","title":"A branch inherits one message fewer than the requested window","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail: `formatInheritedContext > bounds to the last-N whole messages, dropping the oldest entirely` and `formatInheritedContext > respects an explicit lastN bound`. A branch inherits a shorter slice of the parent conversation than the caller asked for, silently losing the oldest message of the window it was promised. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/inherited-context.ts"],"tags":["mcts","context","boundary"]}
{"id":"mcts-pruning-retires-best-branches","title":"Mid-search pruning retires the strong branches and keeps the weak ones","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `pruneLowValueBranches — population + config-honoring gate > a settled low-value node reaches status=pruned mid-search` and `pruneLowValueBranches — population + config-honoring gate > a healthy above-threshold node is never pruned, however many visits`. Mid-search pruning is closing the wrong half of the open population: settled strong branches get retired and their agents aborted, while the branches that have settled below the threshold stay open. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/pruning.ts"],"tags":["mcts","pruning","guard"]}
{"id":"mcts-fail-band-ceiling-too-high","title":"A branch whose code failed can score above the fail band's ceiling","prompt":"Four tests in the core suite fail, including `execution grounding dominates > failing code scores below passing code even when the judge loves both` and `band loophole (WP-A5): prose cannot beat failed-but-attempted code > prose is capped at the fail ceiling when a sibling produced code`. A branch whose code was actually executed and failed now scores above the ceiling the rest of the system pins its acceptance, reflection and prune thresholds to, so failed work escapes its band and a generous judge can rehabilitate it. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/evaluation.ts"],"tags":["mcts","evaluation","default"]}
{"id":"mcts-takes-set-one-too-many","title":"An alternate-takes set offers one candidate more than its cap","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `captureAlternateTakes — the near-tie epsilon rule > duplicate proposal texts dedupe and the set caps at 4 candidates`. A near-tie capture now surfaces more comparable takes than a take set is allowed to carry, because the winner is not counted against the cap that bounds the set. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/takes.ts"],"tags":["mcts","takes","boundary"]}
{"id":"mcts-failed-search-leaves-nodes-pruned","title":"A search that gave up closes its nodes under the wrong status","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `Convergence > BUG-4: returns converged=false when all scores below threshold`. When every branch of a search lands below the acceptance threshold, the leftover open nodes are closed under the wrong terminal status, so a search that genuinely gave up becomes indistinguishable from one whose branches were merely retired mid-search. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/convergence.ts"],"tags":["mcts","convergence","default"]}
{"id":"mcts-tiebreak-tests-codeless-candidates","title":"The convergence tie-break runs its discriminating check over the wrong candidates","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `Convergence > DO-NOW #3: a near-tied candidate that PASSES the discriminating test wins over the marginally-higher-value argmax that FAILS it` and `Convergence > captures near-tied rivals as Alternate Takes before pruning them`. When the judge could not separate the top candidates, the tie-break gathers the wrong subset of them for its execution check, so the near-tie is never actually broken by running anything and value order silently stands. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/test-selection.ts"],"tags":["mcts","test-selection","ties"]}
{"id":"mcts-expansion-spawns-one-branch","title":"Every expansion explores a single branch regardless of configuration","prompt":"Eleven tests in the core suite fail, including `MCTS integration > full cycle: budget=3, branches=2` and `MCTS integration > DO-NOW #1: sibling diversity — each branch in an expansion gets a DISTINCT prompt naming the other branch angles`. However many parallel approaches the caller asks each expansion to compare, the search only ever explores one, so the tree never widens and there is nothing to score branches against. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/engine.ts"],"tags":["mcts","engine","default"]}
{"id":"mcts-resume-checkpoint-swaps-progress","title":"The durable search checkpoint stores iteration count and remaining budget as each other","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `MCTS evict-resume (B6) > an interrupted search resumes from checkpoint, continues remaining budget, converges`. The durable checkpoint a search writes every iteration no longer records how far the loop got and how much budget is left as the values they actually are, so a search re-entered after an eviction resumes against a bogus view of the work remaining. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/search-store.ts"],"tags":["mcts","resume","ordering"]}
{"id":"mcts-strategy-ignores-judge-samples-override","title":"The caller's judge-ensemble size never reaches the evaluator","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `MCTS strategy — stored operator overrides > options.mcts.judgeSamples flows through to the evaluator`. An explicit judge-ensemble size handed to the tree-search strategy is ignored in favour of the built-in default, so the operator's stored spend knob has no effect on how many judge calls each branch costs. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/strategy/mcts.ts"],"tags":["mcts","strategy","default"]}
{"id":"mcts-node-visits-start-at-one","title":"A freshly recorded search node is born already counted as visited","prompt":"Twelve tests in the core suite fail, including `MCTS integration > full cycle: budget=3, branches=2` and `MCTS integration > judge infrastructure failure is backpropagated as 0, not neutral 0.5`. A newly recorded search node starts life as if it had already been sampled once, so the running-mean backpropagation averages every branch's first grounded score against a visit that never happened and every value comes out halved. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/schemas.ts"],"tags":["mcts","schema","default"]}
{"id":"mcts-node-parent-points-at-message","title":"Recorded child nodes do not hang off their parent in the search tree","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail: `MCTS integration > sequential tasks on one DB do not contaminate each other (fresh root per task)` and `MCTS integration > full cycle: budget=3, branches=2`. A child node recorded during an expansion is linked to something that is not its parent search node, so the tree loses its shape — ancestor walks stop at the child and nothing propagates back up to the root. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/record-node.ts"],"tags":["mcts","record-node","ordering"]}
{"id":"required-pairs-rounds-down","title":"Power calculation reports too few paired tasks","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `minimumDetectableEffect > 3pp at that discordance needs far more pairs than the corpus has`. The bench harness's power calculation now advertises a paired-task count that is not actually enough to resolve the effect it was asked about, so a design that cannot see an effect is presented as one that can. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/bench/stats.ts"],"tags":["bench","power","boundary"]}
{"id":"mcnemar-p-uses-all-pairs","title":"Exact paired test is run over the wrong trial count","prompt":"Five tests in the core suite fail, including `pairedBinaryComparison > identical variants produce zero discordance and an honest verdict` and `pairedBinaryComparison > is symmetric: swapping arms flips the sign of the effect`. The exact paired significance test is being handed the wrong number of trials, so two variants that never once disagreed now come back looking like evidence, and swapping the baseline and candidate arms no longer yields the same p-value. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/bench/stats.ts"],"tags":["bench","significance","arithmetic"]}
{"id":"gain-headroom-from-wrong-arm","title":"Normalized gain measures headroom from the wrong arm","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail: `computeGain (stateful vs stateless) > normalizes by remaining headroom` and `gain report > orders the sequence by index so the learning curve reads left to right`. The stateful-versus-stateless gain is normalized against headroom taken from the wrong arm of the comparison, so a run that captured every point of available headroom reports no normalized gain at all. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/bench/stats.ts"],"tags":["bench","gain","arithmetic"]}
{"id":"decision-underpowered-split-guard","title":"Acceptance turns away exactly the splits that can produce evidence","prompt":"Six tests in the core suite fail, including `decideBenchOutcome — rejection by default > a significant held-out improvement is kept, with a power caveat when underpowered` and `decideBenchOutcome — rejection by default > a split too small to reach significance rejects and says to grow it`. The held-out acceptance rule now refuses results from splits that are big enough to establish an effect and tells them to grow the corpus, while splits that could never reach the alpha level are waved through to the remaining checks. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/bench/report.ts"],"tags":["bench","decision","guard"]}
{"id":"candidate-budget-breach-not-counted","title":"Budget breaches by the candidate variant are never counted","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `buildBenchReport > pairs attempts by task and counts budget breaches`. The bench report's breach tally only ever inspects one side of each pair, so an attempt that blew through its compute envelope on the candidate variant is reported as though it stayed inside the budget. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/bench/report.ts"],"tags":["bench","budget","accounting"]}
{"id":"gain-sequence-ordered-backwards","title":"The gain report's learning curve reads back to front","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `gain report > orders the sequence by index so the learning curve reads left to right`. The per-task sequence in the gain report comes out with the last task attempted at the front, so the learning curve is plotted in reverse. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/bench/report.ts"],"tags":["bench","gain","ordering"]}
