{"id":"token-count-accepts-nan","title":"Token accounting propagates a non-finite usage figure","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `run mechanics > usageTokens never returns a non-number, whatever a provider sends`. When a provider reports a usage figure that is a number but not a finite one, the attempt's token total stops being a usable quantity instead of discounting the bad field, which quietly destroys the compute budget the harness pins every attempt to. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/bench/types.ts"],"tags":["bench","budget","guard"]}
{"id":"sealed-validate-flags-the-good-tasks","title":"Sealed-split validation names the well-formed tasks","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `SealedSplit > validate reports only which tasks are malformed`. The held-out corpus's well-formedness pass reports every task that checked out fine and stays silent about the one that did not, so a broken held-out task would never be surfaced. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/bench/split.ts"],"tags":["bench","sealed-split","guard"]}
