{"id":"corpus-error-line-number-off-by-one","title":"Corpus parse errors point at the wrong line","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `eval corpus parsing > throws on invalid JSON with line number`. When an eval corpus file contains a malformed entry, the error names a different line than the one that actually failed to parse, sending whoever has to fix the corpus to the wrong place. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/eval/corpus.ts"],"tags":["eval","corpus","boundary"]}
