{"id":"delegation-loop-overcount","title":"Loop detection charges a repeated block's first pass as wasted motion","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `executionPathSignals — loops > the same call repeated back to back is a loop` and `delegationFeatures > appends a wasted-motion clause only when there is wasted motion`. The deterministic turn-process evidence over-reports how many tool calls the agent spent going in circles: an immediately-repeated block is charged one pass more than it actually wasted. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/delegation-features.ts"],"tags":["delegation-features","arithmetic","boundary"]}
{"id":"delegation-backtrack-self-write","title":"A single tool call counts as backtracking over its own write","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `executionPathSignals — backtracking > a call cannot backtrack over its own write`. The wasted-motion signal now flags a call that writes and reads the same path in one go as if it had undone work an earlier call did. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/delegation-features.ts"],"tags":["delegation-features","ordering","degenerate"]}
{"id":"alignment-precision-inverted","title":"K_align treats wide intervals as readable and precise ones as noise","prompt":"Nine tests in the core suite fail, including `alignmentConvergence > a handful of turns reports its own unreliability instead of a rate` and `renderAlignmentConvergence > marks an interval that is too wide to read`. The correction-rate metric decides backwards whether a rate is precise enough to mean anything: rates measured over a handful of turns are published as findings while the well-measured ones are dismissed. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/alignment.ts"],"tags":["alignment","boundary","degenerate"]}
{"id":"alignment-trend-delta-sign","title":"The alignment trend reports its change with the wrong sign","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `alignmentConvergence > an improving trend: the later interval clears the earlier one` and `renderAlignmentConvergence > shows the rate, its interval, the trend, and every segment`. The correction-rate trend names the right direction but the accompanying change between the two compared scaffold segments points the opposite way, so a genuine improvement is reported as a rise. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/alignment.ts"],"tags":["alignment","arithmetic","ordering"]}
{"id":"changelog-limit-drops-an-entry","title":"The changelog digest returns one entry fewer than asked for","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `buildChangelog — every kind from the seeded ledgers > orders newest first and respects the limit`. The self-change digest silently drops an entry whenever the caller caps how many it wants back. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/changelog.ts"],"tags":["changelog","boundary"]}
