{"id":"web-search-rank-zero-based","title":"Web search results are ranked from zero instead of one","prompt":"Two tests in the core suite fail: `web provider — search > key-less DuckDuckGo path returns ranked results` and `web_search / web_fetch builtins > web_search returns ranked, model-ready text`. The rank each key-less search hit carries is one place off, so the best result no longer presents itself as the first one. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/web/provider.ts"],"tags":["web-search","boundary","arithmetic"]}
{"id":"web-fetch-title-precedence-swapped","title":"A fetched HTML page takes its title from the body heading rather than the document title","prompt":"One test in the core suite fails: `web provider — fetch > HTML page is converted to markdown`. When a fetched page declares a real document title AND has a leading heading in its content, the wrong one of the two is reported back as the page title. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/web/provider.ts"],"tags":["web-fetch","ordering","default"]}
{"id":"wilson-denominator-halved","title":"The Wilson score interval is computed with the wrong correction term","prompt":"Ten tests in the core suite fail, including `wilsonInterval — hand-checked against published values > 3 of 4 → (0.3006, 0.9544)` and `runReplayEval > re-runs labeled turns, scores against recorded outcomes, persists the loss entry`. Every confidence interval the evolution stack reports around a score is now shifted and too narrow, so the numbers claim more precision than the observations support. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/utils/stats.ts"],"tags":["stats","arithmetic","boundary"]}
