{"id":"retry-after-seconds-not-converted","title":"A numeric Retry-After is treated as milliseconds instead of seconds","prompt":"Three tests in the core suite fail, including `withRateLimitRetry > honors Retry-After seconds` and `withRateLimitRetry > gives up at the wall-clock budget and returns the last response`. When a rate-limited provider states exactly how long to hold off, the wait taken is a thousand times shorter than asked for, so the retry hammers straight back. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/providers/rate-limit-retry.ts"],"tags":["rate-limit","arithmetic","default"]}
